WEBVTT

00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:10.880
The history of gaming extends 5,000 
years into the past to ancient Egypt.

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:15.250
Ancient games foretold the 
futures of men and kings.

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:18.950
They were magic ceremonies that 
determined a person's fate.

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:22.930
These ceremonies were known 
as the "Shadow Games."

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.630
In the present, a young boy 
solves the Millennium Puzzle.

00:00:27.010 --> 00:00:29.960
He becomes the heir to the Shadow Games.

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:38.050
This boy possesses two hearts - 
one of light and one of darkness.

00:00:38.570 --> 00:00:41.960
He is known as "Yu-Gi-Oh."

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:50.310
I can't finish reading the magazine pages

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:57.220
I get the feeling that I must read it

00:00:59.110 --> 00:01:03.970
Game cartridges are stacked 
in the corner of the room

00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:10.670
Is there no meaning if I don't play them?

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:15.770
You're on the other side of the table

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:19.140
I'm talking to you, but...

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:26.070
You don't change your 
facial expression at all

00:01:27.010 --> 00:01:32.320
Even though I'm this close to you

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:39.590
These feelings don't reach 
you, don't reach you

00:01:40.010 --> 00:01:46.330
What is truly precious?

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:55.610
Illusionist Faceless Mage's Trap

00:02:00.870 --> 00:02:02.630
How's this, Anzu?

00:02:02.630 --> 00:02:05.370
I attack with Rock Ogre Grotto #1.

00:02:06.870 --> 00:02:11.880
All right!  Happy Lover has 500 defense 
points while Rock Ogre has 800 attack points.

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:13.280
It's destroyed!

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:16.720
It's my turn.  I play a spell card.

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:18.280
I use Breath of Light.

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:20.290
What’s that?

00:02:20.290 --> 00:02:23.290
A divine wind erodes Rock Ogre.

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:25.560
It's reduced to dirt and is destroyed.

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:32.360
Jonouchi, you have 0 life 
points.  I win again.

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:34.410
Jonouchi, you suck.

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:46.490
Yugi, tell me why I can never win.

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:49.610
Jonouchi, show me your deck.

00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:52.420
Here you go.

00:02:56.720 --> 00:02:58.500
What’s this?

00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:01.230
They're all offense-type monsters.

00:03:01.230 --> 00:03:05.040
Yeah!  I put in all my strongest monsters!

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:07.050
That’s not good!

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:13.110
In Duel Monsters, it's important to 
combine spell cards with monster cards.

00:03:13.270 --> 00:03:17.380
If you only use monsters, your opponent's 
spells will easily defeat them.

00:03:17.980 --> 00:03:22.050
Yugi!  Train me in Duel Monsters!

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:30.860
Grandpa, I’m home.

00:03:31.380 --> 00:03:32.590
Welcome home.

00:03:33.260 --> 00:03:36.640
Gramps, how are you feeling?

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:40.870
I’m in great shape.  Are 
you here to buy more cards?

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:44.280
No.  I'm here for Duel Monsters training.

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:47.140
Why all of a sudden?

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:49.370
Because...

00:03:53.980 --> 00:03:59.850
Do you have a crazy dream 
of winning this tournament?

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:02.000
No...

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:05.760
Maybe your goal is to win the 
3,000,000 yen grand prize.

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:09.340
Is that true, Jonouchi?

00:04:09.340 --> 00:04:13.200
Please, Yugi!  I really 
want to win the tournament!

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:16.930
But the tournament begins 
in less than a month.

00:04:17.640 --> 00:04:20.870
I'm willing to help you.

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:22.680
You, Gramps?

00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:25.880
Even though he doesn't look like it, 
Grandpa is a first-rate duelist.

00:04:25.880 --> 00:04:28.150
You didn't need to say the first part.

00:04:28.150 --> 00:04:30.520
But my training is tough!

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:33.090
Understood.  Thank you.

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:37.600
I'll start by changing your attitude about 
entering tournaments because

00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:39.440
you want to win the prize.

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:43.170
I'll teach you about the heart of the cards.

00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:47.010
One more time!

00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:58.540
To the millions of Duel Monsters fans, 
it's time for the tournament finals!

00:04:58.540 --> 00:05:04.550
Among the 200 duelists who won their 
regionals, who will stand at the top?

00:05:04.710 --> 00:05:07.490
Here comes the competitors!

00:05:09.560 --> 00:05:13.970
Representing East Japan, 
14 year-old Insector Haga!

00:05:14.560 --> 00:05:18.610
Representing West Japan, 15 
year-old Dinosaur Ryuzaki!

00:05:20.570 --> 00:05:22.080
Dammit!

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:24.760
I should be the one dueling!

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:26.070
But you did your best.

00:05:26.320 --> 00:05:29.070
You made the quarterfinals of the tournament.

00:05:29.320 --> 00:05:30.440
Well, yeah.

00:05:30.440 --> 00:05:33.610
Your month-long training 
session was very tough.

00:05:38.550 --> 00:05:41.210
Gramps, I can't take it anymore.

00:05:41.950 --> 00:05:44.590
Yes you can!

00:05:44.590 --> 00:05:49.330
Jonouchi!  You can't enter the 
tournament with that attitude!

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:55.050
You made the quarterfinals, but that 
was only in the city qualifiers.

00:05:55.890 --> 00:05:59.170
I’m too ashamed to show my face to Gramps.

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:01.480
What did you say about me?

00:06:01.480 --> 00:06:02.640
Gramps, I’m sorry.

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:05.570
Why?  You did great.

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:14.090
I didn’t think a lazy boy like you would be 
able to enter the tournament, but you worked hard.

00:06:15.890 --> 00:06:16.280
Gramps!

00:06:16.280 --> 00:06:20.390
Yugi, you have a package.

00:06:20.390 --> 00:06:22.600
A package?  From who?

00:06:22.600 --> 00:06:25.530
It doesn’t say.

00:06:26.720 --> 00:06:28.500
I wonder what’s inside.

00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:32.100
Yugi, why didn’t you enter the tournament?

00:06:32.100 --> 00:06:34.870
You could have won it all.

00:06:34.870 --> 00:06:39.110
I decided that I'll only enter 
a tournament when he does.

00:06:39.110 --> 00:06:40.600
You mean Kaiba?

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:46.490
Yeah.  Now that Kaiba knows about the heart of 
the cards, we can battle again fair and square.

00:06:47.290 --> 00:06:50.460
I still don't trust him.

00:06:51.240 --> 00:06:52.960
It already started.

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:55.260
Yugi, who's going to win?

00:06:55.260 --> 00:07:01.810
Insector Haga is good at doing combo attacks 
by combining Insect cards with Armor cards.

00:07:01.810 --> 00:07:08.000
Dinosaur Ryuzaki uses the megaton power of 
his Dinosaur cards to overwhelm his opponent.

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:13.680
If it's bugs versus dinosaurs, then 
Ryuzaki is definitely going to win.

00:07:13.680 --> 00:07:16.320
I wouldn’t be so sure.

00:07:16.320 --> 00:07:20.810
Our battle has been evenly matched so 
far, but I'll finish you with this.

00:07:24.880 --> 00:07:30.810
Dinosaur Ryuzaki summoned Two-Headed King 
Rex, the most powerful Dragon-Type rare card!

00:07:31.900 --> 00:07:33.250
How's that?

00:07:34.240 --> 00:07:36.400
I play this card!

00:07:38.440 --> 00:07:42.710
Insector Haga is fighting 
back with Basic Insect.

00:07:42.880 --> 00:07:45.660
Look at that weak monster.

00:07:45.660 --> 00:07:47.710
Ryuzaki is definitely going to win.

00:07:47.920 --> 00:07:50.720
No, Insector Haga is setting a trap.

00:07:50.880 --> 00:07:54.050
I'll win!  King Rex attacks!

00:07:57.200 --> 00:07:59.580
You just said "attack."

00:07:59.580 --> 00:08:05.230
That keyword activates my 
trap Infinite Dismissal.

00:08:05.230 --> 00:08:07.230
What?  A trap card?

00:08:07.400 --> 00:08:11.570
King Rex is caught in a space-time 
vortex and can’t move.

00:08:15.240 --> 00:08:16.240
King Rex!

00:08:16.440 --> 00:08:18.000
It’s my turn.

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:23.690
I equip Basic Insect with the spell card 
Insect Armor with Laser Cannon Lev. 5.

00:08:30.220 --> 00:08:31.460
Attack!

00:08:36.960 --> 00:08:39.470
King Rex is destroyed.

00:08:41.280 --> 00:08:42.470
I lost.

00:08:42.640 --> 00:08:47.330
The winner is Insector Haga!

00:08:52.980 --> 00:08:55.480
I can’t believe Insector Haga won.

00:08:55.700 --> 00:09:01.800
Insector Haga will now receive the 
championship trophy and money prize.

00:09:01.800 --> 00:09:09.760
Presenting the award is Industrial Illusions 
CEO and the genius creator of Duel Monsters...

00:09:09.760 --> 00:09:13.250
Mr. Pegasus J. Crawford!

00:09:25.010 --> 00:09:26.650
Congratulations.

00:09:26.650 --> 00:09:28.650
Thank you.

00:09:28.650 --> 00:09:34.410
You are granted entry into an upcoming 
event sponsored by my company.

00:09:44.630 --> 00:09:49.640
Pegasus, it seems many elite duelists 
will participate in your event.

00:09:49.840 --> 00:09:55.640
No, there were no duelists in 
this tournament that excited me.

00:09:55.800 --> 00:09:57.080
As for my request?

00:09:57.080 --> 00:10:00.530
It was delivered, just as you ordered.

00:10:01.400 --> 00:10:02.750
I see.

00:10:02.980 --> 00:10:07.200
Yugi, I’m curious about this package.

00:10:07.200 --> 00:10:08.250
Oh yeah.

00:10:08.440 --> 00:10:10.010
What is this?

00:10:11.120 --> 00:10:12.440
What's that?

00:10:12.440 --> 00:10:15.000
Maybe the videotape will have an explanation.

00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:16.980
The videotape?

00:10:16.980 --> 00:10:18.970
Play it.

00:10:26.750 --> 00:10:30.600
Hello.  Nice to meet you, Yugi boy.

00:10:30.600 --> 00:10:31.640
That’s…

00:10:31.640 --> 00:10:33.600
He was just on TV.

00:10:33.600 --> 00:10:37.720
The inventor of Duel Monsters, 
Pegasus J. Crawford.

00:10:37.720 --> 00:10:41.990
This is a video message for Yugi boy.

00:10:43.280 --> 00:10:46.760
I know that you defeated Kaiba boy.

00:10:46.760 --> 00:10:50.240
I will now test your skills.

00:10:50.240 --> 00:10:53.520
But this duel has a time limit.

00:10:53.520 --> 00:10:55.680
We start with 2000 life points.

00:10:55.680 --> 00:11:00.760
After 15 minutes, the player 
with more life points wins.

00:11:00.760 --> 00:11:02.090
Understand?

00:11:02.400 --> 00:11:05.720
He wants you to duel against 
a prerecorded video?

00:11:05.720 --> 00:11:07.290
That's crazy.

00:11:13.000 --> 00:11:16.690
Grandpa!  Jonouchi!  Honda!  Anzu!

00:11:19.640 --> 00:11:21.690
Now no one will bother us.

00:11:21.920 --> 00:11:24.520
Shall we begin, Yugi boy?

00:11:24.520 --> 00:11:26.370
This is a Shadow Game!

00:11:43.020 --> 00:11:45.960
Then I’ll face you.

00:11:45.960 --> 00:11:48.170
Let the duel begin.

00:11:48.990 --> 00:11:51.530
I'll go first.

00:11:52.280 --> 00:11:56.010
I'm done.  It’s your turn, Yugi.

00:11:58.500 --> 00:12:01.040
I’ll play this card.

00:12:01.040 --> 00:12:03.740
That card is Koumori Dragon.

00:12:03.740 --> 00:12:05.060
What?

00:12:05.060 --> 00:12:09.110
I predicted that you would play that card.

00:12:30.610 --> 00:12:37.450
The trap card Dragon Capture Jar seals 
your Koumori Dragon inside this jar.

00:12:46.580 --> 00:12:49.300
Let’s continue the game.

00:12:49.300 --> 00:12:53.920
As long as he has that card on the field, 
I can’t use Dragon-Type monsters.

00:12:53.920 --> 00:13:02.930
Even Kaiba boy's super rare Blue-Eyes White 
Dragon is powerless against this card.

00:13:02.930 --> 00:13:05.160
Blue-Eyes White Dragon?

00:13:05.400 --> 00:13:08.770
This game evolves everyday.

00:13:09.410 --> 00:13:10.920
Then I’ll use this card.

00:13:10.920 --> 00:13:13.770
The Beast-Type monster Silver Fang.

00:13:14.080 --> 00:13:17.590
I predicted you would play 
a Beast-Type monster.

00:13:17.590 --> 00:13:23.170
You're also planning to use Mystical 
Moon to make Silver Fang more ferocious.

00:13:24.710 --> 00:13:28.000
This card is enough to handle Silver Fang.

00:13:28.000 --> 00:13:35.590
Dragon Piper has low attack points, but it 
can break the seal on Dragon Capture Jar.

00:13:35.840 --> 00:13:39.100
You're planning to revive Koumori 
Dragon and take control of it?

00:13:39.320 --> 00:13:41.010
Yes!

00:13:44.000 --> 00:13:48.870
Dragon Piper plays its Flute of 
Resurrection to revive Koumori Dragon.

00:13:48.870 --> 00:13:50.740
My Koumori Dragon!

00:14:00.220 --> 00:14:04.810
You've "played" right into my hands!

00:14:05.480 --> 00:14:08.430
Joke.  It's a joke.

00:14:10.090 --> 00:14:15.160
Yugi boy, I know you're 
shocked, but this is real.

00:14:15.160 --> 00:14:16.940
You cannot beat me.

00:14:17.160 --> 00:14:21.440
When you lose, you will have to 
participate in the event I'm sponsoring.

00:14:21.600 --> 00:14:22.660
What?

00:14:22.660 --> 00:14:28.350
The event will prove who is 
the true king of the duelists.

00:14:28.350 --> 00:14:30.200
King of the duelists?

00:14:30.200 --> 00:14:36.690
Yes.  And the king will win a large 
money prize and great prestige.

00:14:36.690 --> 00:14:39.130
I’m not interested in your event.

00:14:39.440 --> 00:14:40.830
What if I refuse?

00:14:40.830 --> 00:14:44.300
No no, you can't refuse.

00:14:44.300 --> 00:14:49.130
Since you can't defeat me, you 
can't avoid this situation.

00:14:49.130 --> 00:14:51.200
I haven’t lost yet.

00:14:51.200 --> 00:14:54.650
Okay.  Let's continue the game.

00:14:55.910 --> 00:14:58.220
I end my turn.

00:14:58.220 --> 00:15:00.850
Yugi boy, it's your turn.

00:15:01.020 --> 00:15:07.370
There has to be a reason why Pegasus 
can see my hand.  What is it?

00:15:12.840 --> 00:15:16.570
I’ll use this card to destroy Dragon Piper.

00:15:18.710 --> 00:15:22.840
Hold on.  Did I choose this card 
or only thinking that I did?

00:15:22.840 --> 00:15:27.050
What if he’s using magic to control me?

00:15:30.370 --> 00:15:35.240
What if he's using hypnotism to control me?

00:15:35.240 --> 00:15:38.490
Then it would appear as 
if he was seeing my hand.

00:15:38.760 --> 00:15:41.850
I figured out his magic trick.

00:15:41.850 --> 00:15:45.080
Yugi boy, it's your turn.

00:15:45.080 --> 00:15:49.530
If I choose a card in my hand, 
I’ll be controlled by his magic.

00:15:50.190 --> 00:15:52.230
I have to put faith in my deck.

00:15:52.480 --> 00:15:54.930
I'll risk everything on my next card.

00:15:57.310 --> 00:16:00.470
There's no need to declare an attack.

00:16:00.470 --> 00:16:03.480
Your next card is a Zombie-Type monster.

00:16:03.480 --> 00:16:06.200
I activate my trap Sun Shower!

00:16:06.200 --> 00:16:10.660
The flood of sunlight kills 
all Zombie-Type monsters.

00:16:10.660 --> 00:16:14.080
I knew there was a limit to your magic.

00:16:14.080 --> 00:16:19.370
You can see my hand, but you can't see the 
cards that I draw directly from my deck.

00:16:20.050 --> 00:16:21.830
My card is…

00:16:22.560 --> 00:16:24.290
Dark Magician!

00:16:25.320 --> 00:16:28.600
That's not a Zombie-Type monster.

00:16:28.600 --> 00:16:32.840
Dark Magician attacks Koumori Dragon!

00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:36.360
Why aren't you attacking Dragon Piper?

00:16:36.360 --> 00:16:38.680
I'll take care of my own cards.

00:16:38.680 --> 00:16:43.130
Because if the game ends while it's 
under enemy control, that's cruel.

00:16:43.570 --> 00:16:46.320
Those feelings will prove fatal.

00:16:51.000 --> 00:16:52.320
Black Magic!

00:17:01.720 --> 00:17:07.810
Okay.  You succeeded in figuring 
out some of my powers.

00:17:07.810 --> 00:17:11.310
But you underestimate my powers.

00:17:11.560 --> 00:17:12.580
What?

00:17:12.580 --> 00:17:14.850
It's my turn.

00:17:16.530 --> 00:17:18.470
Unbelievable!

00:17:18.470 --> 00:17:21.690
This card is Illusionist Faceless Mage.

00:17:21.900 --> 00:17:24.360
I've never seen that rare card before.

00:17:24.360 --> 00:17:27.930
However, Dark Magician is the 
strongest Spellcaster-Type monster.

00:17:27.930 --> 00:17:33.730
I use Eye of Illusion to unleash 
a combo attack on Dark Magician.

00:17:34.930 --> 00:17:36.380
I'll take it on!

00:17:36.380 --> 00:17:39.210
Dark Magician, Black Magic!

00:17:39.440 --> 00:17:42.510
The illusionary spell Eyes of Illusion!

00:17:46.110 --> 00:17:47.730
Who won?

00:17:49.050 --> 00:17:50.530
A tie?

00:17:50.980 --> 00:17:53.800
In a tie, both monsters should be destroyed.

00:17:53.800 --> 00:17:56.620
Is this due to Eyes of Illusion's effect?

00:17:57.480 --> 00:18:00.490
There are 5 minutes left 
until the counter reaches 0.

00:18:00.490 --> 00:18:05.500
If I don't battle and preserve 
my life points, I win.

00:18:05.500 --> 00:18:08.660
But only a coward would choose that route.

00:18:08.660 --> 00:18:10.500
I’ll fight to the end!

00:18:10.720 --> 00:18:15.490
I can only truly win by lowering 
Pegasus's life points to 0.

00:18:15.490 --> 00:18:18.760
Celtic Guardian attacks 
Illusionist Faceless Mage!

00:18:18.760 --> 00:18:23.320
Since Celtic Guardian has more attack 
points, it will win the fight.

00:18:23.320 --> 00:18:25.580
Wow, you fell for it.

00:18:25.580 --> 00:18:30.820
Eyes of Illusion does more than increase 
Illusionist Faceless Mage's attack points.

00:18:30.820 --> 00:18:32.170
What?

00:18:37.750 --> 00:18:40.170
Why was Celtic Guardian destroyed?

00:18:43.180 --> 00:18:44.700
You're...

00:18:44.700 --> 00:18:46.660
Dark Magician!

00:18:46.660 --> 00:18:53.030
Oh no!  Due to Eyes of Illusion, Dark 
Magician is under his control for this turn!

00:18:53.030 --> 00:18:56.980
Pegasus knows every card in my hand.

00:18:56.980 --> 00:19:01.750
I end my turn, and time is almost up.

00:19:02.000 --> 00:19:04.810
Nice fight, Yugi boy.

00:19:05.720 --> 00:19:07.800
The game isn’t over yet.

00:19:07.800 --> 00:19:11.970
My final card is the 
Fiend-Type Summoned Skull!

00:19:13.070 --> 00:19:14.400
Battle!

00:19:21.800 --> 00:19:23.600
Game over.

00:19:23.600 --> 00:19:28.850
That was close.  I would've 
lost if that battle took place.

00:19:28.850 --> 00:19:34.240
Yugi boy, you're more skilled than I thought.

00:19:34.240 --> 00:19:38.810
I sense that we will battle 
again at Duelist Kingdom.

00:19:38.810 --> 00:19:40.930
And if I refuse?

00:19:42.160 --> 00:19:45.490
You cannot escape me.

00:19:47.600 --> 00:19:51.370
I possess the Millennium Eye's shadow power.

00:19:51.370 --> 00:19:53.000
Millennium Eye?

00:19:53.000 --> 00:19:58.880
Let's meet again at the Kingdom if you 
want to reclaim what’s most dear to you.

00:20:11.680 --> 00:20:13.250
Yugi!

00:20:14.990 --> 00:20:16.040
Yugi!

00:20:16.040 --> 00:20:17.210
Grandpa!

00:20:19.920 --> 00:20:28.650
Grandpa!

00:20:32.480 --> 00:20:39.030
Yugi enters the Duelist Kingdom Tournament 
to get his grandpa's soul back from Pegasus.

00:20:39.550 --> 00:20:43.440
Wait!  We won't let you go alone, Yugi!

00:20:43.440 --> 00:20:47.830
Joey, you can't enter 
since you weren't invited.

00:20:48.020 --> 00:20:50.560
What?  You're doing it for your sister?

00:20:50.560 --> 00:20:54.420
Everyone on the ship has their own goals, 
but there's a trap waiting for Yugi.

00:20:54.420 --> 00:20:57.720
